Careful with my added assertion: `assert.equal(plan.filter(item => !item.reads.length && !item.cropIds.length && !item.payload.topics).length, 1, ...)` — are there other evidence-free packets here? Packets: source (reads ✓), teaching group (reads + payload.topics ✓), coherence (no reads, no crops, no topics ✓), visual ×2 (crops ✓). So exactly 1 ✓.

Now the question checks. Let me rewrite the three checks.

Check 1 (line ~197): "Question review reads its source and blocks a unique correct-option explanation cue":

```js
await check("Question review reads its source and blocks a unique correct-option explanation cue", async () => {
  const proposed = { ... };  // keep
  const bad = { ... };       // keep
  const requests = [];
  const options = fixture(async (_selected, context) => { requests.push(structuredClone(context)); return message(bad); });
  const before = structuredClone(proposed);
  await assert.rejects(reviewLearnQuestion(options, proposed, [1]), /Repair the proposed question.*revealing the answer/s);
  assert.deepEqual(proposed, before);
  assert.equal(requests.length, 2, "an unchanged question review is one request per attempt");   // hmm: reviewTargetQuestion retries once on failure → but a "changes" verdict is not a failure → 1 request.
```
Wait: `reviewTargetQuestion` calls reviewOne once; if `result.failure` → retry. A "changes" verdict (status changes, no failure) → no retry → 1 request ✓ then throws "Repair the proposed question...". So `requests.length === 1`.

Hmm — careful: `reviewLearnQuestion` wraps `reviewTargetQuestion`. Let me check what reviewLearnQuestion does (learn-review.ts:229+). It calls reviewTargetQuestion with options and returns a guard. Any extra layer? Let me check lines 220-260 of learn-review.ts to be certain about the wrapper (also for Step 9).

Also: the plan verification item 3 says "assert exactly one `modelRegistry.complete` call per question review, `tools.length === 0` and `messages.length === 2`, for both the pass and the changes verdict".

So:
```js
  const requests = [];
  const options = fixture(async (_selected, context) => { requests.push(structuredClone(context)); return message(bad); });
  const before = structuredClone(proposed);
  await assert.rejects(reviewLearnQuestion(options, proposed, [1]), /Repair the proposed question.*revealing the answer/s);
  assert.deepEqual(proposed, before);
  assert.equal(requests.length, 1, "one request answers the question review");
  assert.deepEqual(requests[0].tools, [], "a prepared question review has no tool loop");
  assert.equal(requests[0].messages.length, 2, "its prompt and prepared evidence are all it sees");
  assert.deepEqual(options.observations.reads, [[1, 1]]);
  assert.deepEqual(options.observations.views, [], "a text question needs no rendered page");
  assert.deepEqual(options.observations.crops, [], "a text question needs no crop image");
```
and drop the `await assert.rejects(reviewLearnQuestion(fixture(), proposed, [1]), /read page 1/)` line (impossible now) — replace with a check that a prepared question review that cannot read its page fails as evidence:
```js
  const unreadable = fixture(); unreadable.evidence.read = async () => "[Page 1] truncated";
  await assert.rejects(reviewLearnQuestion(unreadable, proposed, [1]), /Question review incomplete/);
```
Hmm, that would produce failure "evidence" → retry once → second failure → throws "Question review incomplete (evidence)..." ✓ good, and asserts the guard still pending. This preserves the spirit (missing evidence blocks the question) with the new mechanics. Note: with prepared, evidence failure is caught in prepareEvidence → ReviewerRunError("evidence", ...) → reviewOne returns incomplete("evidence") → reviewTargetQuestion retries → fails again → throws `Question review incomplete (evidence)`. ✓ 

Careful: the evidence read returns text without "[Page 1]" marker → in the *prepared* path, collect() calls tools[0].execute("prepared", args, stop) which throws Error("Source page 1 was not returned...") → caught and re-thrown as ReviewerRunError("evidence", "Required source evidence could not be prepared.") ✓ code "evidence" ✓.

Check 2: "Question approval requires its source figure and full page, without unrelated-page requirements" →
```js
await check("Question approval prepares its figure evidence, and a text question stays text only", async () => {
  const figureQuestion = { question: "Use the field arrows in the figure to explain the flux.", kind: "conceptual" };
  const textQuestion = { question: "Explain why zero divergence does not imply zero field.", kind: "conceptual" };
