  const textGuard = await reviewLearnQuestion(text, textQuestion, [1]);
  assert.doesNotThrow(() => textGuard(text.section));
  assert.deepEqual(text.observations, { reads: [[1, 1]], views: [], crops: [] }, "a text question review carries the page text and no images");
});
```
This drops the "omitted tool call" cases ✓ per plan. But it removes coverage that a reviewer omitting evidence is blocked — that's now covered by prepared-evidence completeness (assert: the review fails if a required crop can't be loaded)? For a figure question, requiredViews = [1] and crops = [crop-1]; the prepared path calls view(1) and crop(crop-1) ✓; if the crop load fails, evidence error ✓. I can add one negative: figure fixture whose `evidence.crop` throws → reviewLearnQuestion rejects with /Question review incomplete/.

Check 3: "Question approval rejects lesson, source-plan and figure changes before display" → replace `fixture(withTools(assessmentCalls()))` with `fixture()` (verdict pass by default). And keep the rest ✓. Note the check also asserts `legacy.observations.reads` = [] ✓ (no-op path).

